From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:52:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] js: a GC task no helper has started runs on the thread that
 joins it

GitHub still hung the daemon with 0109 in (2026-11-13, TouchPad, stacks read with ptrace): the
main thread in GCRuntime::beginSweepingZoneGroup -> joinTask(sweepAtomsTask) waiting, both
helper threads in off-thread parses blocked in AutoLockForExclusiveAccess, which the GC holds
through the slice. The sweep task sat on the worklist with no helper free to take it.

GCParallelTask::joinWithLockHeld now takes its task off the worklist when no helper has started
it and runs it on the joining thread (never on a helper); only a task a helper is running is
waited for.
---
 js/src/vm/HelperThreads.cpp | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/js/src/vm/HelperThreads.cpp b/js/src/vm/HelperThreads.cpp
index 0b765a9e23..bd5b231970 100644
--- a/js/src/vm/HelperThreads.cpp
+++ b/js/src/vm/HelperThreads.cpp
@@ -1151,6 +1151,26 @@ js::GCParallelTask::joinWithLockHeld(AutoLockHelperThreadState& locked)
     if (state == NotStarted)
         return;
 
+    // A task no helper has started runs here: the GC joins its sweep tasks while it holds the
+    // exclusive-access lock, and off-thread parses on every helper can be waiting for that lock.
+    if (!CurrentHelperThread()) {
+        GlobalHelperThreadState::GCParallelTaskVector& worklist = HelperThreadState().gcParallelWorklist(locked);
+        for (size_t i = 0; i < worklist.length(); i++) {
+            if (worklist[i] != this)
+                continue;
+            worklist.erase(&worklist[i]);
+            {
+                AutoUnlockHelperThreadState unlock(locked);
+                uint64_t timeStart = PRMJ_Now();
+                runTask();
+                duration_ = PRMJ_Now() - timeStart;
+            }
+            state = NotStarted;
+            cancel_ = false;
+            return;
+        }
+    }
+
     while (state != Finished)
         HelperThreadState().wait(locked, GlobalHelperThreadState::CONSUMER);
     state = NotStarted;
